  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Pandaroside I and HepG2 through a series of target interactions. Pandaroside I is identified as a target of multiple compounds, including MIP, Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside, and Camelliquercetiside B, all of which are implicated in targeting HepG2. These findings indicate that Pandaroside I may act as a mediator in the signaling pathways leading to HepG2 cell response, possibly through the activation of downstream targets such as ent-Intermedeol. The consistent scores across the three paths, with a final score of 0.5088 in two of them, suggest a reliable association, though the lower score in the third path may reflect variability in the evidence or the specific context of the target compound. The mechanisms appear to involve the modulation of cellular processes that influence HepG2, though the exact pathways remain to be fully elucidated.",
